# IAF Donchian 48H Volatility Breakout

## Source
- Source: [[sources/github-topic-algorithmic-trading-python]]
- Topic URL: https://github.com/topics/algorithmic-trading?l=python
- Repository: `coding-kitties/investing-algorithm-framework`, organization `coding-kitties`
- Repo URL: https://github.com/coding-kitties/investing-algorithm-framework
- Strategy file: https://github.com/coding-kitties/investing-algorithm-framework/blob/main/examples/strategies_showcase/07_event_driven_signal/strategy.py
- README: https://github.com/coding-kitties/investing-algorithm-framework/blob/main/examples/strategies_showcase/07_event_driven_signal/README.md
- Source citation: 2026 URL review, exact strategy file at https://github.com/coding-kitties/investing-algorithm-framework/blob/main/examples/strategies_showcase/07_event_driven_signal/strategy.py
- Target symbols: EURUSD.DWX, XAUUSD.DWX, GER40.DWX for the initial DWX port.

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Timeframe: H1 bars.
- For each bar, compute the prior 48-bar high using completed bars only.
- Open long when flat and current close is above the prior 48-bar high.

### Exit
- Compute the prior 48-bar low using completed bars only.
- Close long when current close is below the prior 48-bar low.

### Stop Loss
- Source has no explicit stop. V5 build should add default catastrophic `2.0 * ATR(14)` stop.

### Position Sizing
- Source uses available-cash all-in example sizing. V5 baseline uses fixed $1,000 risk and one position per magic.

### Additional filters
- No source filter. Port BTC/EUR H1 event-driven example to liquid DWX FX, metals, and index CFDs.

